cctext patch 0001: conditional processing (<switch>, systemLanguage,
requiredExtensions).

Upstream lunasvg ignores <switch> and renders every child, so draw.io
exports (a <foreignObject> with HTML labels and a <text> fallback inside a
<switch>) drew both, or nothing readable. <switch> now parses as a <g> that
keeps only its first child whose conditions pass, for an "en" user agent
with no extensions: requiredExtensions is always false (an empty list is
false too, SVG 1.1), systemLanguage matches a primary tag "en",
requiredFeatures is always true (dropped in SVG 2; Chrome and resvg agree).
Conditions are read from the start tag without consuming it. Paint servers,
<defs>, <clipPath>, <mask>, <marker>, <style>, <symbol> and <stop> are not
conditional (SVG 1.1 section 5.8). A failing element is skipped like an
unknown one.

Apply (from the repository root, onto the pristine upstream files):
  patch -p1 -d third_party/lunasvg < third_party/lunasvg/patches/0001-switch-conditional-processing.patch

